From: RNS-Gate maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: sunxi: preserve a watchdog started by U-Boot

Gate starts the watchdog in U-Boot so a trial kernel that hangs cannot
exhaust the A/B fallback mechanism. Let watchdog core feed a running timer
until userspace opens it, instead of disabling it unconditionally at probe.
The Gate bootloader uses the driver's maximum timeout of 16 seconds.

--- a/drivers/watchdog/sunxi_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/sunxi_wdt.c
@@ -275,7 +275,13 @@ static int sunxi_wdt_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	watchdog_set_drvdata(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev, sunxi_wdt);
 
-	sunxi_wdt_stop(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev);
+	if (readl(sunxi_wdt->wdt_base + sunxi_wdt->wdt_regs->wdt_mode) &
+	    WDT_MODE_EN) {
+		set_bit(WDOG_HW_RUNNING, &sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev.status);
+		sunxi_wdt_ping(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev);
+	} else {
+		sunxi_wdt_stop(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev);
+	}
 
 	watchdog_stop_on_reboot(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev);
 	err = devm_watchdog_register_device(dev, &sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev);
